Let's find a recursive formula for $g(n)$.

- The first term is Naledi's initial altitude, which is $\blue{40}$ meters above sea level.
- The common difference is the distance Naledi climbed each hour, which is $\pink{10}$ meters.

Therefore, this is the recursive definition of the sequence:

$\begin{cases}
g(1)=\blue{40}
\\\\
g(n)=g(n-1)+\pink{10}
\end{cases}$

In conclusion, $g$ is an *arithmetic* sequence.

$\begin{cases}
g(1)=\blue{40}
\\\\
g(n)=g(n-1)+\pink{10}
\end{cases}$
